WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.100
To Earth

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.000
Welcome back!

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.110
If they're allowed to brag just because
they're the Titans...!

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.150
Even <i>I</i> can do that!

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.690
Are you boarding without introducing
yourself?

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.860
I guess you don't have to.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.230
You're well known for flying out and
returning without doing a thing.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.770
Because you're a member of the Titans,
I had greater expectations of you.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.440
The warships we're presently pursuing are the
Argama and Mont Blanc.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.610
It appears that they're heading for either
Side 1, Side 2, or the Moon.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.710
In addition, they will be taking a course close
to the Earth and attempt...

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.730
...to attack our defense satellite
on the way there.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.160
In which case...

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.800
- No significant changes?
- No, sir!

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.400
Perhaps their reduction in speed
is meant to let our guard down.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.710
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.940
They're probably
in the midst of regrouping their forces.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.210
Likely.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.710
What is our present location?

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:36.010
Sir!

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.080
We'll reach the laser defense satellite
network in about twenty-five minutes!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.680
So, are we going through with this?

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.750
Ensign Reccoa was already convinced by
Commodore Blex that she's going.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:49.160
Ensign Reccoa? Can she do it?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.830
Really. A mobile suit?

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.890
Astonaige.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.770
- Never mind.
- Sorry.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.670
I've got work to do, so let me use it.
Is this the Gundam Mk. II?

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.670
No.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:09.840
It must be a tough job to try to collect all
parts of Lieutenant Quattro's Rick Dias.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.380
Thanks to that, the rebuilding
of the Gundams has got to wait.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.180
This is really well-designed!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.450
I designed it after the Mk. II and Dias
and added a new armor.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.930
I even gave it a name, the Zeta Gundam.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.300
You can certainly tell that you're a Newtype.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.240
That has nothing to do with it.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.790
You're right on with the calculations.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.670
- Just a fluke.
- Huh?

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.140
- Let me hold onto the disk.
- S-Sure.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.310
Why do you have to hide it?

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.620
Miss Reccoa.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.050
Are you sure about this?

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.820
The capsule's really well made,
so there's nothing to worry about.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.730
I'm referring to your duty. Actually...!

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.990
It's a job that even I could fulfill.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.170
Kamille?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.880
Who is it?

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.740
What do you want, Kamille?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.340
Can't I visit you without a reason?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.440
I just came to chat.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:52.380
Please come in.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.380
Just remember...

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.920
...if you've come here looking for
sympathy, you won't get any from me.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.290
You and I aren't in any sort of relationship.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.890
Never mind!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:08.230
I only wanted to ask why someone like you
was with the Titans.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:11.900
Kamille!

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.830
Here's your disk back.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.640
What are you doing here?

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.480
Kamille!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.570
He doesn't mean any harm, Ensign Reccoa.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.350
I think I understand.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:29.390
Pardon?

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.450
What a bleak room.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.490
I'm here on probation, after all.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.890
Could I ask you to take care
of the plants in my room?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.430
There isn't much time left.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.100
Not much time?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.070
I'm disembarking from the Argama.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.430
I've located Ensign Reccoa, sir.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.040
She's in the room of Lieutenant Emma
on probation.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.510
Lieutenant Emma's room?

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:56.280
An observation room?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.940
Turn up the volume!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:03.610
<i>I cannot return to the Titans,</i>
<i>and I don't even want to.</i>

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.160
<i>However...</i>

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.790
<i>I don't see any reason why the A.E.U.G.</i>
<i>has to be this belligerent.</i>

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:13.190
<i>Anyone can see that doing this</i>
<i>will surely lead to an all-out war.</i>

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.670
Was it really necessary
to open fire on Green Oasis...

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.800
...and endanger the lives of
innocent people?

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.670
Compared to people behind
the Colony 30 Incident...

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:27.270
...what we did was almost nothing.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.640
The Colony 30 Incident?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.480
Side 1's Colony 30 held a rally against
the Earth Government.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.210
What do you think Bask Om did
to suppress it?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.560
G3. Poison gas!

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.660
He used poison gas in a colony?

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:50.860
Impossible!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.130
Poison gas in a colony?

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.670
That sounds like something Zeon would do.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:00.340
<i>But the use of G3 was prohibited after</i>
<i>the colony drop that began the last war!</i>

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.000
<i>It couldn't have been used!</i>

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.950
I imagine she's finding this
extremely difficult to believe.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.420
Especially because she was just thrown
onto the totally opposite side.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.690
We might need to show her
what happened at Colony 30.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.620
Yes.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:18.190
She has the makings of a good pilot.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.760
- For the A.E.U.G.?
- Of course.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.030
I had no idea either.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.110
- Cool!
- Awesome!

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.540
In addition, as a member of the Titans,
even if your rank remains the same...

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.770
...you will be recognized as having one
rank higher than that of the regular military.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.080
Which means we get three extra days
of paid holidays a month!

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.550
You're right.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.120
How indulgent!

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.520
That's why we end up
with wimps like you, Lieutenant.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.360
Then I will have you all
take part in this operation...

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.030
...with Lieutenant Jerid as your
team leader.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.490
Why Lieutenant Jerid?!

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.430
I have much more experience
out here in space.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:02.600
I told you. Titan officers have a rank higher.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:04.980
Yes, sir!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.550
Wait!

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.410
What? Did you come to laugh at me?

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.450
I understand how you feel,
but you won't beat me.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.800
You're so simple-minded to come here
and add to your embarrassment.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:34.240
Why can't Earthnoids understand the
difference between the Earth and space?

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.270
Why is it?!

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.000
Why is what?

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.340
I trained sufficiently on Earth.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:41.570
My ability to adjust is superb...

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.410
...and that's why I was able
to join the Titans.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.080
The ability to adjust
is different from the ability to cope.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:48.940
Tell me! Why?!

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:50.790
Don't touch me!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.890
As long as you continue acting like a
brute, you'll never beat me.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.090
Wh-Why do you say that acting this way
is brutal?

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.290
Now you're getting on my nerves.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.630
Such ways of doing and saying things
are all <i>your</i> way, right?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.290
You're not considering
other people's feelings!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.600
You're not going to get any closer to me...

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:09.110
...treating me like you treated
the other women in your life.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.110
I didn't mean to give that impression.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:15.380
With each new atmosphere, each new partner,
and each new situation...

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.480
...a different response is required of you!

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.810
But I believe I've always done that.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.820
You haven't seen a thing yet.
What do you expect to change?

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.320
Are you implying
that I haven't seen anything yet?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.060
If you had...

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:31.220
...you should've been victorious
against that Gundam Mk. II.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:35.770
Then tell me!

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:37.300
I want to defeat that bastard!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.340
Why?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.000
Why?!

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:46.540
I have thoughts of one day
leading the Titans!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.470
To do that, I must swallow my pride
and learn from this!

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.520
You seem serious.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:58.180
Okay, then commence operations
from the Bosnia.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.360
From your ship?

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.360
I'll teach you something.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:15.170
You're late.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.210
I'm sorry!

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.200
Lieutenant Quattro, were you aware
of the Colony 30 Incident?

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:22.180
Yes.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.550
I knew nothing more than
that there was some sort of riot.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.010
It was much more than that.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.610
Why was there a riot?

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.590
Because humans cannot trust other people.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.920
They don't trust others,
so they doubt each other.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.550
They doubt each other, so they
eventually think others are wrong...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.430
...and this forces them
to make wrong choices.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.400
Then Lieutenant Quattro, do you fight
because you don't trust others?

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:46.730
No, I fight because the Titans
are running out of control.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.670
Then what am I to do?

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.500
What do you feel you should do?

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.980
Right now, I think I'm doing the right thing.

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:54.740
Then it is the right thing.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.250
What's happening with Ensign Reccoa?

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:58.680
Oh...

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.040
...she's descending to the Earth.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.260
Oh...

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.490
...she's descending to the Earth.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.370
She's entering the Earth's atmosphere
in a capsule.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.340
If you need to tell her something,
now would be the time.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.740
Right!

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:26.640
He reminds me of Amuro Ray.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.540
How's the capsule?

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:29.550
No problems!

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.840
She's a tough girl,
but I can tell she's nervous.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.910
She can descend
with her eyes closed if she wants...

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:38.790
...as long as no one gets in our way 
the moment we launch the capsule.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.850
Yes. The enemy must be aware now...

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.520
...that we plan on destroying either
their defense satellite or solar battery.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:45.860
You're right.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.160
Is Lieutenant Quattro
prepared to launch yet?!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.580
Listen, my troops will take off first.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:06.280
I know.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.880
In outer space,
you must focus on all directions!

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:13.320
I must sense the enemy's hostility through
the armor of the mobile suit, right?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:14.830
<i>That's what I'm saying.</i>

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:29.700
"Emanate your mind through the vacuum
of space," huh?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.040
- How much more time?
- You still have plenty of time.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:40.580
Thank you.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.380
Please leave me alone for a moment.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.420
Yes, Ensign!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.260
Where's Ensign Reccoa?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.060
Ensign, are you going alone?

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.890
This thing only fits one person.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.060
- Ensign.
- Yes?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.400
Ensign...!

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.870
We're on level two battle stations!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.910
Don't you have anything better to do?

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.780
Opening airlock.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:13.180
Right.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.720
Lower the visor!

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.920
Apolly! Roberto!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.490
We're taking a direct route
after attacking the solar battery!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.700
- <i>Roger!</i>
- Roger!

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:36.810
Here we go!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.940
<i>Course is clear! Go ahead!</i>

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.550
Enemy craft detected!

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.920
These things happen!
We can't bring them back now!

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.680
Open the laser circuit!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:58.730
Set your coordinates
on the Rick Dias troop!

00:14:59.060 --> 00:14:59.500
That's impossible!

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.160
Don't say that until you've tried!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:07.100
Another way to live life is to hold back
when the time is right to hold back.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.000
All so that one can
achieve greater success later!

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.810
Have we caught up with the enemy?

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:19.940
Quattro's unit will reach the air defense
area of the solar battery in ten seconds.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:20.780
Okay.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.340
Do we still not have
a laser circuit connection?!

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.180
Not yet, sir.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.250
Hurry.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.370
Don't get hit, Apolly.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.100
If it's going to come to this anyway...!

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.390
GM unit from the Mont Blanc.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:07.830
Attack the enemy fleet directly!

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.330
Bringing the Hohsenka
up to the catapult deck.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.270
Okay!

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:14.960
Raise the elevator!

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.840
<i>The Hohsenka will be launched</i>
<i>according to plan!</i>

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.800
But the enemy's approaching!
This is ridiculous!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.950
Ensign Reccoa, don't worry.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.920
We'll safely send you off
in the direction of Jaburo.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.580
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.180
Only one left!

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.770
Hey, Kamille! What are you up to now?!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.460
I'm going out! Please raise the elevator.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.600
<i>Don't overdo it!</i>
<i>What good will you be out there?!</i>

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.530
Where's Lieutenant Quattro?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.600
He's headed to the inner orbit
defense satellite!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:55.710
<i>There are three enemy units...</i>
<i>No, six or seven!</i>

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.010
<i>Kamille's in a disassembled Gundam?!</i>

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.510
Kamille is?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.210
<i>Enemy units are close by, right?!</i>

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.120
<i>This is the Hohsenka! Reccoa speaking!</i>

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.880
<i>Would you like to get off and rest a bit?</i>

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:06.790
<i>No, sir!</i>

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.320
Is she descending to Earth?

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.950
<i>It can still be used!</i>

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.730
<i>Hand me the rifle!</i>

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.390
<i>We must ensure Miss Reccoa</i>
<i>launches safely, mustn't we?!</i>

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:17.500
<i>Astonaige, let Kamille handle the situation!</i>

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:18.740
Silly boy.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:19.970
<i>Here they come!</i>

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.080
That must be it!

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.210
Boy, we're finally here.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.020
Let's see!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.420
They're here!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.990
Isn't she afraid of the enemy firing at her?
She's hardly looking around!

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.940
She's sensing the enemy hostility?!

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.780
Incredible!

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:05.980
Kamille's going out?

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.350
<i>Kamille. Don't fall into the</i>
<i>Earth's gravity well!</i>

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.390
Roger! Kamille, let's do it!

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.990
The Mont Blanc?!

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:26.860
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.340
- I see flashes from explosions behind us!
- Explosions?!

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.480
We're under enemy attack!

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.350
Where's Quattro's unit?

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:40.580
They're returning.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.350
Destroy them!
Why can't we destroy them?!

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.590
Okay! How many seconds
until we launch the capsule?

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.150
Ninety seconds!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.560
There should still be time
before the capsule's launch.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.370
The Mont Blanc...!

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:12.580
What was that light?

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.420
Who is it? Who's calling out to me?

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:26.730
Mr. Amuro.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:29.360
We're experiencing a power failure.
Would you still like some tea?

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:31.270
I'll have it out here.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:32.630
Yes, sir!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.540
Reinforcements?

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:40.240
No wonder they were hardly retaliating!
Their forces were split up!

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:41.770
How long until the capsule launches?

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.440
Captain Henken,
what's going to happen?

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:51.820
Kamille!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.320
A Rick Dias?!

00:19:58.860 --> 00:19:59.920
Missed it!

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:04.300
Damn it!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.530
Out of my way!

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.440
<i>Sixty seconds to capsule launch.</i>

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:13.770
Miss Reccoa.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.270
Dodged it?!

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.650
Is he the pilot of the red Rick Dias?

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.610
This isn't good!

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.020
Unless I get away from here,
Miss Reccoa will...!

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:28.290
Kamille?!

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:29.160
He's taking part in an actual battle?!

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:32.560
Captain Henken!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.390
<i>We're making final adjustments</i>
<i>to the course.</i>

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.560
<i>Commence countdown!</i>

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.460
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:37.190
<i>I must force the enemy away...</i>

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:40.430
- <i>...from the Argama...!</i>
- Kamille! That boy...

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.770
Blast it!

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.370
Okay, Kamille! Well done!

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.280
Course set!

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:50.210
Ready to launch capsule!

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.490
Not yet?!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.790
Counting down.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:00.720
Ten...

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:11.540
- <i>Three, two, one, zero.</i>
- Three, two, one, zero!

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.230
- She's out!
- Good!

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:25.250
There you are!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:44.360
Kamille. Thank you.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.500
<i>I don't want to lose.</i>

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:53.540
Jerid?

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.450
<i>Someday...</i>

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:58.350
...I'll defeat him with my own hands.

00:21:58.780 --> 00:21:59.940
No matter what!

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:05.690
Is that boy Kamille
piloting that Gundam Mk. II?

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:07.960
Then is he a Newtype?

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:16.200
You've gone to Earth, Miss Reccoa...

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:23.030
Later that evening...

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:28.210
...an unusual number of shooting stars
were observed across Central America.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:31.410
It was caused by the sinking
of the Mont Blanc.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.630 --> 00:23:49.300
Lila was determined to only fight
under absolutely favorable conditions.

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:53.860
However, the nightmare of the Side 1
Colony 30 Incident draws her to death.

00:23:54.140 --> 00:23:58.100
The shot fired by the Gundam Mk. II
makes its way through Lila.

00:23:58.650 --> 00:24:02.450
And Kamille hears the requiem for Lila.

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:07.490
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Escape from Side One".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Escape from Side One

00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:11.090
You will see the tears of time.
